# Distributed run log (mandatory)

Multiple machines edit this repo. **Do not** edit `report/track_a.tex` or `report/track_b.tex` unless the user **explicitly asks** you to (e.g. “update the LaTeX logbook”, “edit track_a.tex”). Default: markdown log only. That avoids merge conflicts.

## Your log file (and only yours)

Resolve paths at runtime — **never hardcode** another user or host:

```bash
RUN_LOG_USER="$(whoami)"
RUN_LOG_HOST="$(hostname | cut -d. -f1)"
RUN_LOG_FILE="report/${RUN_LOG_USER}/${RUN_LOG_HOST}.md"
```

Examples: `report/romain.poggi/rouget.md`, `report/thomas.turkieh/sole.md`.

| Rule | Action |
|------|--------|
| **Write** | Only `report/$(whoami)/$(hostname-first-label).md` |
| **Forbidden (unless user explicitly asks)** | `report/track_a.tex`, `report/track_b.tex`, `report/main.tex` |
| **Forbidden (always)** | any `report/{other_user}/`, any `report/{you}/{other_host}.md`; editing **`experiments/**`** when only logging |

Create `report/$(whoami)/` if missing. **Append** a new section per experiment event; do not rewrite prior sections except to update **status/metrics** on the **latest** entry for the same run name.

## When to log (required)

On **start**, **stop**, **finish**, or **submit** of a training / long eval / submission job the user cares about:

1. Resolve `RUN_LOG_FILE` with the commands above.
2. **Prepend** a new section at the top of the file (below the file header), separated by `---`.
3. If the same **run name** already has an open `RUNNING` block at the top, you may **update that block only** (status, metrics) instead of duplicating.

Skip logging only if the user says not to report, or the change is trivial (typo, refactor) with no experiment outcome.

## Section format (strict)

Each entry:

```markdown
---

## {Short descriptive title} | Track {A|B|A+B} | {YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM}

- **Status:** RUNNING | DONE | FAILED | STOPPED
- **Run:** {run_name or experiment id}
- **Experiment:** [`{experiments_doc_stem}`](../../experiments/{experiments_doc_stem}.md) — link to the **experiments/** spec (read-only); **never** line numbers or in-file anchors
- **Hydra:** `experiment={preset}` (plain text; config lives under `configs/experiment/`, not linked from here)
- **Log:** [`{log_basename}`](../../logs/{track_dir}/{log_basename}) — under `logs/track_a/`, `logs/track_b/`, or study dir (see start-resume-runs rule)
- **W&B:** [run]({url}) — long train/pretrain only; omit for submit/short jobs
- **PID:** [`{pid}`](../../logs/…/file.pid) — only while **RUNNING** and a pid file exists; remove pid file when done
- **Ckpt:** `{path}` (target or best)
- **Metrics:** {one line: val/LB/holdout only — no code, no hyperparameter essays}
- **Submit:** `{csv path}` → LB **{score}** (if applicable)
```

- **Track:** exactly `A`, `B`, or `A+B`.
- **Date/time:** local wall clock when you write the entry (`date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M'`).
- **Metrics:** results only (e.g. `best val top1=0.5358 ep50 EMA`, `LB 53.71%`). Use the project glossary symbols (`T`, `lr`, `E`, `bs`) sparingly on one line if needed.
- **Do not** explain implementation, YAML keys, or code changes in this file.

## Experiment references (`experiments/` — read-only when logging)

Run specs and result write-ups live under **`experiments/*.md`**, not in `configs/experiment/` (Hydra YAML only).

- **Link** the relevant doc from your log: `` [`experiment_16052026`](../../experiments/experiment_16052026.md) `` (path from `report/{user}/{host}.md`, two levels below repo root).
- Pick the **most specific** `experiments/*.md` that scopes the run (batch instruction, ablation plan, TTA results, etc.). Index: [`experiments.md`](../../experiments/experiments.md).
- **Do not** cite line numbers (`L42`, `#L42`, `:42`) — those files evolve.
- **Do not edit** any file under `experiments/` when you are only logging a run; reference only.
- Mention the Hydra preset as plain text: `` **Hydra:** `experiment=track_a_foo` `` — do **not** link to `configs/experiment/*.yaml` from the run log.
- If no dedicated doc exists, link the closest parent spec or note `` (no dedicated experiments/*.md) ``.

## File header (create once)

If the file does not exist:

```markdown
# Run log — {user} @ {host}

Machine-local experiment log. Other hosts/users have their own files under `report/{user}/{host}.md`. Do not edit this file from another account or machine.

```

## LaTeX report (`track_a.tex`, `track_b.tex`, `main.tex`)

- **Only if the user explicitly asks** may you modify `report/track_a.tex` or `report/track_b.tex` (or consolidate narrative into `main.tex`).
- Otherwise treat shared LaTeX as **read-only** for run logging.
- Compiling `report/main.tex` is **not** required when you only touch `report/{user}/{host}.md`.

## Cross-rule: launching runs

When **starting or resuming** training, follow **`.cursor/rules/start-resume-runs.mdc`** (log naming, `logs/track_a|b/`, header with start date + `experiment_doc`, health check, W&B resume, pid cleanup). This file is only for **outcome/status** after launch.

## Quick check before commit

```bash
git diff --name-only | grep -E '^report/(track_[ab]\.tex|main\.tex)$' && echo 'STOP: shared LaTeX touched' || true
```
